        "photo2": {
          "type": "photo_review",
          "settings": {
            "image_url": "",
            "body": "The lagree shoes are fantastic for reformer Pilates as well as mat Pilates and barre. No more concerns about slipping means better performance. Absolutely love them!",
            "author": "Fedra P.",
            "location": "Widnes, GB",
            "rating": 5
          }
        },
        "photo3": {
          "type": "photo_review",
          "settings": {
            "image_url": "",
            "body": "I use these Grippys exclusively for Pilates and have turned many on to them! They are perfect for no slip and precision and I'm a 7–8 class a week person and have 2 pairs that I lightly clean with the same gentle wipes we use for equipment.",
            "author": "Lauren",
            "location": "Indianapolis, US",
            "rating": 5
          }
        },
        "text1": {
          "type": "text_review",
          "settings": {
            "body": "My love-hate relationship with the sock has finally come to a ceremonial end. The vast improvement during the first minute of barre class, with my new Barreletics performance skin shoes, is beyond words.",
            "author": "Mia Evans",
            "location": "Verified Purchase",
            "rating": 5
          }
        },
        "text2": {
          "type": "text_review",
          "settings": {
            "body": "This pair is my second purchased — my first having been purchased almost 4 years ago. The reason for the second pair is purely color! I must say these are truly valuable to my Pilates practice — I refuse to wear anything else — the security is unmatched.",
            "author": "Kimberly",
            "location": "Knoxville, US",
            "rating": 5
          }
        },
        "text3": {
          "type": "text_review",
          "settings": {
            "body": "The best invention known to Pilates devotees. I am 70 years old and I am able to accomplish several advanced moves on the Cadillac apparatus. Namely, the parakeet, the complete parakeet. If you know anything about Pilates, you know that your foot has to be gripping the bar without fail.",
            "author": "Dvorah S.",
            "location": "Fairfield, US",
            "rating": 5
          }
        },
        "text4": {
          "type": "text_review",
          "settings": {
            "body": "I was looking for a 'good' pair of Pilates socks and came across what I thought was a ridiculously priced alternative. I sat on the idea for a couple of weeks but finally decided to take the plunge. After my first class… [game changer].",
            "author": "Wendy B.",
            "location": "Grayslake, US",
            "rating": 5
          }
        },
        "text5": {
          "type": "text_review",
          "settings": {
            "body": "At 68, I can do my Pilates and yoga with much more precision and control because I know I won't slip.",
            "author": "Sarah D.",
            "location": "Fruita, US",
            "rating": 5
          }
        },
        "text6": {
          "type": "text_review",
          "settings": {
            "body": "I feel so much more stable and safe during my Lagree sessions. Colors are fun too so they are compliment magnets! Well worth the money spent!",
            "author": "Anna W.",
            "location": "Fullerton, US",
            "rating": 5
          }
        }
