    "collection-faq": {
      "type": "collection-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "f1": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What's the difference between Closed Sole and Open Sole?",
            "answer": "<p><strong>Closed Sole</strong> — heel and foot fully covered. <strong>Open Sole</strong> — heel exposed, mid-foot breathing hole. More grounded, barefoot feel. Natural toe splay. Both perform identically — same grip, same stability. Choice is preference and feel only. Same $74.</p>"
          }
        },
        "f2": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Tired of Pilates socks and yoga socks that slip?",
            "answer": "<p>Pilates socks, yoga socks, and barre grip socks rely on silicone dots that peel and fabric that stretches. Performance Skins replace that category with full-underfoot grippy shoes — Secure in Every Hold through flat back chair, water ski, chair pose, reformer footwork series, and Megaformer Super Lunge — without mid-set resets. Not another disposable sock.</p>"
          }
        },
        "f3": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Best alternative to Pilates socks, yoga socks & barre grip socks?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes — that's the job. Traditional barre grip socks and Pilates socks absorb sweat and lose traction in weeks. One Performance Skin pair (Closed Sole or Open Sole, $74) holds through footwork series, water ski, Super Lunge, Catfish, and heated rooms without the sock-replacement cycle. Full-contact 360° grip instead of dots — built for barre, Classical and reformer Pilates, Cadillac, Megaformer, Lagree, yoga, and hot Pilates. Both soles perform identically — same grip, same stability.</p>"
          }
        },
        "f4": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Which machines and disciplines are they built for?",
            "answer": "<p>Barre, mat Pilates, Classical Pilates, reformer, Cadillac (trapeze table), Chair, Tower, Megaformer, Lagree, yoga, hot yoga, and hot Pilates. Same 360° grip whether you're on the carriage, holding the Cadillac bar (parakeet / push-through), digging into Super Lunges on Megaformer, or flowing on the mat. Closed Sole and Open Sole both perform identically across every discipline — choice is preference and feel only.</p>"
          }
        },
        "f5": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Reformer, Cadillac, Chair & Tower — will they hold on Classical apparatus?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. On the reformer: footwork series (toes, arches, heels, tendon stretch), elephant, knee stretches, and the long stretch series demand continuous underfoot contact. On the Cadillac / trapeze table: push-through and parakeet need grip that holds the bar — not a sock that slides off mid-exercise. Bridging and footwork on the Chair or reformer stay locked without sock resets. Same grip system in Closed Sole or Open Sole.</p>"
          }
        },
        "f6": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Megaformer, Lagree & barre — named moves that punish grip socks?",
            "answer": "<p>Megaformer and Lagree: Super Lunge, Elevator Lunge, Catfish, Bear, and Plank to Pike load the foot laterally — silicone-dot socks slide. At the barre: flat back chair, water ski, relevé, plié, and seat-work pulses need feet that don't walk out of the hold. Same 360° grip system in every color above.</p>"
          }
        },
        "f7": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I wear a sock with them?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Optional. A sock made for Performance Skins with grip around the toes — for sweat, warmth, comfort, or when the studio wants a sock. The Skin is still the grip. Both soles perform identically — same grip, same stability. Choice is preference and feel only.</p>"
          }
        },
        "f8": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Yoga flows — chair pose to downward dog?",
            "answer": "<p>From chair pose (Utkatasana) and warrior to downward dog and standing balances — grip that holds through every transition. Closed Sole or Open Sole — same $74 system as barre and Pilates. Both perform identically — same grip, same stability. Choice is preference and feel only.</p>"
          }
        },
        "f9": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How do I clean them?",
            "answer": "<p>Hand wash with warm soapy water. That's it.</p>"
          }
        },
        "f10": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What size should I order?",
            "answer": "<p>M and L ship today; Small is coming soon. Use the size chart above the grid. Between sizes? Most studio practitioners size up for comfort.</p>"
          }
        },
        "f11": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What's your return and warranty policy?",
            "answer": "<p>30-day returns on items in new, sellable condition. 90-day warranty against manufacturing defects (not normal wear). Free shipping on orders over $150. Ships in 1–2 days.</p>"
          }
        },
